    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "`plan_extraction` is implemented in `solution.py` and the test suite in `tests/test_solution.py` passes: `python -m pytest -q tests` reports 38 passed. I did not measure line coverage, since only the test command was allowed, but every line and branch of `solution.py` is exercised by a test I wrote. The code follows `spec.md`: `dest` is validated and stripped of trailing slashes, and both `/` and `\\` act as separators. Each member is normalised (empty and `.` segments dropped, `..` popping one segment), and it is rejected if it contains NUL, is absolute, has a drive prefix, climbs above the destination, or normalises to nothing. Directory entries are validated but left out of the result. File members are checked case-insensitively for collisions, and the result is returned in input order or not at all. `UnsafePathError` is kept as a `ValueError` subclass, and the stub's signatures and class name are unchanged. The one judgement call is that a directory entry never counts as a collision with a file of the same name, because the spec only mentions file-to-file duplicates.",
